Task 7.9 — Controlled Selection-Stage Analysis Using Frozen Task 7.8 Results

OBJECTIVE

Determine whether the downstream evidence-selection stage is responsible for excluding useful medical evidence that has already passed reranker eligibility.

This is a controlled diagnostic experiment only.

Do NOT replace the reranker.
Do NOT change retrieval.
Do NOT change eligibility thresholds.
Do NOT change production behavior.
Do NOT add medical data.
Do NOT use benchmark labels or hidden DDXPlus labels.

The specific motivating finding is the Task 7.8/7.8.1 result:

Panic Disorder evidence became eligible under MedCPT but was not selected.
Flu evidence became eligible and was selected.
Asthma evidence showed both eligibility and selection regressions.
Task 7.8.1 source-text review found 22 clearly useful newly-positive pairs and 31 ambiguous pairs among the 60 newly-positive transitions.

The purpose of Task 7.9 is to determine whether useful eligible evidence is being lost primarily because of the existing selection/diversity/document-budget logic.

